   "attributes": {
    "biography": {
     "en": "**Name In Native Language:** 道満晴明 (Douman Seiman)\n\n**Also Known As:** Iijima Susumu (飯島進)\n\n**Birth:** March 7\n**Years active:** 1993-Present\n**Hometown:** Chiba, Japan\n\n**Circles:** \nG Kun Dow (ジークンドー)\nKiheitai (畸兵隊)\n\nHis current art style was directly influenced by Mike Mignola (Dowman is a fan of Hellboy).\n\nAn avid fan of horror movies (the witches in Voynich Hotel were named after an obscure Italian horror trilogy). After graduating from a design vocational school, he made his debut in the publishing section of BANDAI drawing manga for videogame anthologies.\n\nHis pen name is based on the two legendary onmyouji, Abe no Seimei and Ashiya Doman."
    },
